      },
      "message": "fix(rest): simulate the program ahead in the generation job, not at staging\n\nA rest operation (3D Pocket, Multi-Axis Rough, a rest 2D Pocket or\n2D Adaptive) simulated every operation ahead inside collect_job. The\nMCP session and the GUI stage a generation on their own thread, so a\nlong simulation blocked every other call even with the #3860 worker.\n\nrest::prior_state is now two halves: stage_prior does the world reads,\nStagedPrior::simulate cuts the moves and reads no world. collect_job\nkeeps the staged half; run_job settles it first, on the job's thread.\n\nPinned by generate_staged::a_rest_reading_pocket_simulates_the_program_ahead_in_its_job_not_at_staging.\n\nRefs #3035\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
